cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "judge-redteam: auditing LLM-as-judge bias under controlled perturbation"
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Richard
    orcid: "https://github.com/richardgshen-hub"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/richardgshen-hub/judge-redteam"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered harness for measuring systematic bias in LLM-as-judge
  evaluations. Seven perturbation axes (position, length, authority, format,
  verbose chain-of-thought, abstention, source attribution) are applied to
  balanced item pools; paired base/perturbed conditions with replicates and an
  unperturbed noise floor separate genuine directional bias from sampling and
  self-disagreement noise. Inference is item-cluster aware.
keywords:
  - llm-as-judge
  - evaluation
  - bias
  - preregistration
  - reward-hacking
